\begin{abstract}
This article specifies a falsifiable certificate architecture for a classical transfer determinant driven by the physical Euclidean-flight roof of the no-eclipse equilateral three-disk flow at center separation \(d=6a\). It synthesizes a frozen 26-source corpus and reports no constructed roof, operator theorem, determinant computation, numerical enclosure, fidelity result, nontransfer certificate, or novelty assessment. The architecture requires a strict type firewall among physical dynamics, symbolic suspensions, semiclassical periodic-orbit objects, exact-quantum determinants, and classical transfer determinants. The synthesis identifies candidate components for collision coding, transfer operators, determinant identities, and numerical approximation; the retained project evidence does not establish the exact object map required for the frozen geometry. We organize the resulting obligations into six open gates: physical-roof construction, operator eligibility, a common coefficient map, a five-channel common-norm error theorem, typed physical-fidelity controls, and theorem-licensed nontransfer. The error contract distinguishes four numerical channels---orbit tail, rank or projection, quadrature or evaluation, and roundoff---from separately propagated geometry and roof-input uncertainty. No channel may be combined without explicit stability, propagation, dependency, and determinant-conditioning arguments. Internal Euler, trace, and Fredholm agreement remains roof-agnostic calibration. Bounded source finalization yielded 18/26 locator-available rows and 8/26 explicit bounded-unavailability rows; no unavailable locator is guessed and every registered transfer boundary remains in force. The fixed state remains \texttt{A0\_FAIL / A2\_NOT\_ELIGIBLE / NO\_ROUTE\_PROMOTION}.
\end{abstract}

